      "dom_id": "question-64868",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the value of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡({180}^{∘}).$",
      "worked_solution": "The angle ${180}^{∘}$ is a quadrantal angle. Let's draw out the quadrantal angles on the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254920/assets/792a778286533d589a3410223aaf197b07e64ea77566042d7bb8ac13fbad9768.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle ${180}^{∘}$ corresponds to the point $(-1,0).$\n\n- Since the cosine of the angle corresponds to the $x$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{cos}⁡({180}^{∘})=-1.$\n\n- Since the sine of the angle corresponds to the $y$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{sin}⁡({180}^{∘})=0.$\n\nTherefore, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡({180}^{∘})=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡({180}^{∘})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({180}^{∘})}=\\frac{-1}{0}.\n$$\n\nHowever, division by zero is undefined. Therefore, $\\operatorname{cot}⁡({180}^{∘})$ is undefined.",
